# Source: shipped-complex-borrows
# Metal-ammine complexes borrowed verbatim (log_k only) from llnl.dat, which
# ships in vendor/iphreeqc/database but is not a routed database. No reaction enthalpy
# (reaction heat stays declared unpriced), no rate, no spectrum. 25 C, I = 0.
# Exception, stated on its row: the nitrous acid protonation carries llnl's
# stated reaction enthalpy (a datum, not a "Not possible to calculate" hole).
SOLUTION_SPECIES
    # llnl.dat lines 9413-9433 (zinc ammines)
    Zn+2 + NH3 = Zn(NH3)+2
        log_k 2.0527
    Zn+2 + 2 NH3 = Zn(NH3)2+2
        log_k 4.259
    Zn+2 + 3 NH3 = Zn(NH3)3+2
        log_k 6.4653
    Zn+2 + 4 NH3 = Zn(NH3)4+2
        log_k 8.3738
    # llnl.dat lines 2277-2293 (cadmium ammines)
    Cd+2 + NH3 = Cd(NH3)+2
        log_k 2.5295
    Cd+2 + 2 NH3 = Cd(NH3)2+2
        log_k 4.876
    Cd+2 + 4 NH3 = Cd(NH3)4+2
        log_k 7.2914
    # llnl.dat lines 4549-4552 (nitrous acid). Every route that loads this
    # file (wateq4f, minteq.v4) defines NO2- as its N(3) master species but
    # no protonated form, so acidified nitrite had no weak-acid buffer.
    # log_k 3.2206 is llnl's stated value (pKa 3.22; the NBS 1982 tables
    # give 3.22 too, see kerotakis-core nitrogen_oxides.rs). The stated
    # -delta_H -14.782 kJ/mol is carried (NBS: -14.6). llnl's -analytic fit
    # is NOT taken: it evaluates to 3.232 at 25 C, disagreeing with the
    # stated log_k. Matter books back under NO2- (no registry HNO2), the
    # citrate/thiosulfate precedent; the pH sees the buffer.
    NO2- + H+ = HNO2
        log_k 3.2206
        -delta_H -14.782 kJ/mol
